*Linux Commands:

1. hostname --> It will display server name
2. ping --> It is used to check server is pingable(Server up or down) or not.
3. clear --> To clear the screen
4. ls --> short listing. It will display files
5. ll --> Long listing. It will display files
6. touch  --> It is used to create file
7. mkdir --> To create directory
8. rmdir --> To remove empty directory
9. ls-ltr  --> It lists the files in ascending order based on time (latest)
10.ls -lrt --> It lists files in descending order
   ls -lt --> It lists files in descending order
11. ls -laas  --> It lists all files including hidden files which are present in server.
12. vi filename  --> We can able to create a file, edit a file or view a file.
13. cat  --> It is used to create a file, add a data into file. We can see data in a file. 
14. rm -rf dirname  --> To remove files/directories forcefully
15. pwd: present working directory  --> To see current path 
16. cd .. --> To change the current directory. By using this we can come one step back i.e parent directory
17. cp --> To copy data from one file to another file/another directory
18. mv --> 1. To move a file from one place to another place. 2. To rename a file
19. cd --> to change directory
20. rm --> To remove a file
21. df  --> To check disk utilisation 
22. df -m --> It displays disk utilisation in MB format
23. df -h  --> It displays disk utilisation in human readable format
24. du -sh --> displays size of a file
25. du -sh * --> to check all files size at a time
26. > filename --> To delete/reduce a data without deleting the file
27. history  --> To see history of commands which we executed
28. gzip --> To compress a file
29. gunzip  --> To uncompress a file
30. sudo su --> To switch to root user
