32. df -TH /dev --> to check disk utilisation for /dev filesystem and its type of filesystem
33. rm -rf dnf.* --> to remove a all files which starts with dnf.
34. echo 1 >  /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches --> To reduce memory utilisation
35. echo 2 >  /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches --> To reduce memory utilisation
36. echo 3 >  /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches --> To reduce memory utilisation
37. free  --> to check memory utilisation in kb format
38. free -m --> it displays memory utilisation in MB format
39. free -h --> displays memory utilisation in human readable format
40. TOP --> To see system running processor, system load average, uptime,how many users logged in
41. Kill -9 PID.  --> To kill a processor
42. iostat --> to check cpu utilisation
43. vmstat --> to check cpu utilisation
44. ps -ef | grep httpd  --> to check process/application is running or not
45. service httpd status --> to check a service status
46. service httpd start --> to start a service
47. service httpd stop --> to stop a service
48. service httpd restart --> to restart/running a service
49. yum install httpd --> to install a service
50. ps --> to see list of processors
51. ps -ef --> shows present background OS running processors and its information
